{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"the-backyard-safari","version":1,"title":"The Backyard Safari","ageTiers":["5-6","7-8"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"Dela had two empty paper tubes, some string and a notebook. ‘Today we are going on safari,’ she told her little brother Edo. ‘We will see wild animals!’","sentences":["Dela had two empty paper tubes, some string and a notebook.","‘Today we are going on safari,’ she told her little brother Edo.","‘We will see wild animals!’"],"image":"sha256:b91363c7434c6be75c7c7892ad02fba53a5370de539195c20441dbbf9706d67d","alt":"A girl holds up paper-tube binoculars in a sunny yard while her brother holds a bucket.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:5c6923590848587b8a2e6c796e6b6f744f38e45cbc154166f63967eca6d88cb2","durationMs":14280,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5896],[5896,11884],[11884,14280]],"words":[[0,369],[369,645],[645,921],[921,1382],[1382,1843],[1843,2764],[2764,3133],[3133,3686],[3686,3962],[3962,4146],[4146,5896],[5896,6357],[6357,6541],[6541,6817],[6817,7278],[7278,7462],[7462,8475],[8475,8751],[8751,9120],[9120,9396],[9396,9949],[9949,10594],[10594,11884],[11884,12068],[12068,12437],[12437,12713],[12713,13082],[13082,14280]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"First they crouched by the garden wall. Dela peered through her tubes. ‘I see an ant!’ She counted its legs. One, two, three, four, five, six. ‘An ant has six legs.’","sentences":["First they crouched by the garden wall.","Dela peered through her tubes.","‘I see an ant!’ She counted its legs.","One, two, three, four, five, six.","‘An ant has six legs.’"],"image":"sha256:07f688ebc5d1e7e702dfd50f30cffaf7b351cb532d5824cdd30c0ce7974be520","alt":"The children crouch over a line of ants near a wall; the girl counts on her fingers.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:19c47b77c86cbcd2172c3516c7863375c9966898fe9b0c1244b7a469e331d4c7","durationMs":18840,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3913],[3913,7189],[7189,11648],[11648,16926],[16926,18840]],"words":[[0,455],[455,819],[819,1547],[1547,1729],[1729,2002],[2002,2548],[2548,3913],[3913,4277],[4277,4823],[4823,5460],[5460,5733],[5733,7189],[7189,7371],[7371,7644],[7644,7826],[7826,9100],[9100,9373],[9373,10010],[10010,10283],[10283,11648],[11648,12376],[12376,13104],[13104,14014],[14014,14833],[14833,15652],[15652,16926],[16926,17108],[17108,17381],[17381,17654],[17654,17927],[17927,18840]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"Next, under a leaf, they found a shiny beetle. Dela counted. Six legs again. ‘So the ant and the beetle are both insects,’ she wrote. ‘Insects have six legs.’","sentences":["Next, under a leaf, they found a shiny beetle.","Dela counted.","Six legs again.","‘So the ant and the beetle are both insects,’ she wrote.","‘Insects have six legs.’"],"image":"sha256:c17561bba12e7ae47b4929c00f2ed707dab380d9b337a0150f4e9903115ca35b","alt":"The girl lifts a leaf to reveal a shiny beetle and writes in her notebook.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:534b5ad9449fecf8198ed68a668d4e09df010c081dd8a0b3637ffe7b2b3fef08","durationMs":14680,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4603],[4603,6348],[6348,8173],[8173,12775],[12775,14680]],"words":[[0,714],[714,1111],[1111,1270],[1270,1984],[1984,2301],[2301,2698],[2698,2857],[2857,3254],[3254,4603],[4603,4920],[4920,6348],[6348,6586],[6586,6903],[6903,8173],[8173,8332],[8332,8570],[8570,8808],[8808,9046],[9046,9284],[9284,9760],[9760,9998],[9998,10315],[10315,11267],[11267,11505],[11505,12775],[12775,13330],[13330,13647],[13647,13885],[13885,14680]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"On the water pot, a snail slid along slowly. ‘It has no legs at all!’ said Edo. ‘Just one big foot.’ Dela giggled. ‘A snail is not an insect.’","sentences":["On the water pot, a snail slid along slowly.","‘It has no legs at all!’ said Edo.","‘Just one big foot.’ Dela giggled.","‘A snail is not an insect.’"],"image":"sha256:90286196a993588380abf46faa43c28ec879f096c0312968ef5ab2f08566726b","alt":"A snail travels slowly on a clay pot while the boy points and laughs.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:430688ce981e0491234d6227b2dcd603495da1ecaf8d947e217d8f6bbae0909c","durationMs":14720,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,4443],[4443,8360],[8360,12453],[12453,14720]],"words":[[0,174],[174,435],[435,871],[871,1568],[1568,1742],[1742,2178],[2178,2526],[2526,2962],[2962,4443],[4443,4617],[4617,4878],[4878,5052],[5052,5400],[5400,5574],[5574,6793],[6793,7141],[7141,8360],[8360,8708],[8708,8969],[8969,9230],[9230,10537],[10537,10885],[10885,12453],[12453,12627],[12627,13063],[13063,13237],[13237,13498],[13498,13672],[13672,14720]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"Then Edo found a spider spinning a web between two sticks. Dela counted. ‘One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight! A spider has eight legs.’ ‘So a spider is not an insect either,’ said Edo.","sentences":["Then Edo found a spider spinning a web between two sticks.","Dela counted.","‘One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight!","A spider has eight legs.’ ‘So a spider is not an insect either,’ said Edo."],"image":"sha256:74dc7df8f80b61f92e16ae3193c92251ddcb5ea0d61f2c63453955ad2c268288","alt":"A spider hangs in the centre of a web between two sticks as the children watch.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:a6c968e4f7a01cfef66694e5a661f99ae7257d2c3af8e79942c2c79da6a7b00b","durationMs":22720,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5727],[5727,7827],[7827,15274],[15274,22720]],"words":[[0,382],[382,668],[668,1145],[1145,1336],[1336,1909],[1909,2673],[2673,2864],[2864,3150],[3150,3818],[3818,4104],[4104,5727],[5727,6109],[6109,7827],[7827,8591],[8591,9355],[9355,10310],[10310,11169],[11169,12028],[12028,12792],[12792,13747],[13747,15274],[15274,15465],[15465,16038],[16038,16324],[16324,16801],[16801,18233],[18233,18424],[18424,18615],[18615,19188],[19188,19379],[19379,19665],[19665,19856],[19856,20429],[20429,21479],[21479,21861],[21861,22720]]}}},{"n":6,"text":"Edo reached for the spider. ‘No,’ said Dela. ‘On safari, we look and do not touch. We do not know which small animals might bite, and we must not hurt them.’ Edo put his hand behind his back.","sentences":["Edo reached for the spider.","‘No,’ said Dela.","‘On safari, we look and do not touch.","We do not know which small animals might bite, and we must not hurt them.’ Edo put his hand behind his back."],"image":"sha256:08b4f00a4d3389e0bdd2cc5ada8809963ff5b53447e0071f82cc26b46738085e","alt":"The girl gently holds her brother’s hand away from a spider.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:47a50eae9b7e503b880cc1017397c72d3f0968c0969e57b3e29d6f7d9895484e","durationMs":16480,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,2627],[2627,4696],[4696,8119],[8119,16480]],"words":[[0,239],[239,796],[796,1035],[1035,1274],[1274,2627],[2627,3184],[3184,3502],[3502,4696],[4696,4855],[4855,5731],[5731,5890],[5890,6208],[6208,6447],[6447,6606],[6606,6845],[6845,8119],[8119,8278],[8278,8437],[8437,8676],[8676,8994],[8994,9392],[9392,9790],[9790,10347],[10347,10745],[10745,11462],[11462,11701],[11701,11860],[11860,12178],[12178,12417],[12417,12735],[12735,13929],[13929,14168],[14168,14407],[14407,14646],[14646,14964],[14964,15442],[15442,15681],[15681,16480]]}}},{"n":7,"text":"They drew a chart in the notebook. Ant: 6 legs, beetle: 6 legs, snail: 0 legs, spider: 8 legs. Mama came over and smiled. ‘Which animal has the most legs?’ ‘The spider!’ said Edo.","sentences":["They drew a chart in the notebook.","Ant: 6 legs, beetle: 6 legs, snail: 0 legs, spider: 8 legs.","Mama came over and smiled.","‘Which animal has the most legs?’ ‘The spider!’ said Edo."],"image":"sha256:389812aa561df09904cfd46ae995ac8fa7e772b3af0476c9e0bd3734aa68fb24","alt":"A chart with four animals and numbers of legs is drawn in a notebook.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:176c35d44635d7bc1a5086a427f166bb9a6788f2d68c98c230a1efdccbfa46af","durationMs":18320,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3106],[3106,10274],[10274,12824],[12824,18320]],"words":[[0,319],[319,638],[638,797],[797,1195],[1195,1354],[1354,1593],[1593,3106],[3106,3743],[3743,3902],[3902,4619],[4619,5495],[5495,5654],[5654,6371],[6371,7168],[7168,7327],[7327,8044],[8044,8920],[8920,9079],[9079,10274],[10274,10593],[10593,10912],[10912,11231],[11231,11470],[11470,12824],[12824,13222],[13222,13700],[13700,13939],[13939,14178],[14178,14497],[14497,15692],[15692,15931],[15931,17285],[17285,17604],[17604,18320]]}}},{"n":8,"text":"That night Dela wrote on the last page: ‘The best safari was in our own yard. There is more to see when we look carefully.’ The end.","sentences":["That night Dela wrote on the last page: ‘The best safari was in our own yard.","There is more to see when we look carefully.’ The end."],"image":"sha256:98cfe0fe30f6faf01f5559763486f3fd11abfc27c0772792833ba55ce9747cba","alt":"The girl writes in her notebook by lamplight with her tube binoculars beside her.","audio":{"hash":"sha256:facb8a3baa8efab4c7a85689cb9733697462aadcc933143e8782b9841e9f2994","durationMs":13840,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,7802],[7802,13840]],"words":[[0,416],[416,936],[936,1352],[1352,1872],[1872,2080],[2080,2392],[2392,2808],[2808,3745],[3745,4057],[4057,4473],[4473,5097],[5097,5409],[5409,5617],[5617,5929],[5929,6241],[6241,7802],[7802,8322],[8322,8530],[8530,8946],[8946,9154],[9154,9466],[9466,9882],[9882,10090],[10090,10506],[10506,12587],[12587,12899],[12899,13840]]}}}],"activities":[{"id":"safari-c1","type":"comprehension","afterPage":2,"question":"How many legs does an ant have?","options":["Six","Eight","Four"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"safari-c2","type":"comprehension","afterPage":5,"question":"How many legs does a spider have?","options":["Eight","Six","Ten"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"safari-voc","type":"vocabulary","afterPage":3,"word":"insects","definition":"Small animals with six legs and three body parts.","distractors":["Animals with eight legs","Animals with no legs"]},{"id":"safari-ph","type":"phonics","afterPage":5,"targetSound":"sn","prompt":"Which words start with the sn sound, like snail?","options":["snail","slid","spider","sticks"],"correctIndexes":[0]},{"id":"safari-p1","type":"prediction","afterPage":6,"prompt":"Edo wants to touch the spider. What should Dela say? Tell a friend.","options":["Look and do not touch","Go ahead","Pick it up"]},{"id":"safari-s1","type":"sequencing","afterPage":8,"prompt":"Put the safari in order.","items":["They saw an ant.","They found a snail.","They saw a spider.","They made a chart."]},{"id":"safari-sel","type":"sel","afterPage":8,"prompt":"Dela felt curious and careful. How do you feel when you explore somewhere new?","feelingOptions":["Curious","Careful","Excited","Nervous"]}],"glossary":[{"word":"safari","definition":"A journey to look at wild animals.","pages":[1,8]},{"word":"insects","definition":"Small animals with six legs.","pages":[3]},{"word":"spider","definition":"A small animal with eight legs that often makes a web.","pages":[5]}],"assets":{"sha256:5c6923590848587b8a2e6c796e6b6f744f38e45cbc154166f63967eca6d88cb2":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/5c6923590848.mp3","bytes":57549,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:b91363c7434c6be75c7c7892ad02fba53a5370de539195c20441dbbf9706d67d":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/the-backyard-safari/page1-1.webp","bytes":86852,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:19c47b77c86cbcd2172c3516c7863375c9966898fe9b0c1244b7a469e331d4c7":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/19c47b77c86c.mp3","bytes":75789,"type":"audio/mpeg"},"sha256:07f688ebc5d1e7e702dfd50f30cffaf7b351cb532d5824cdd30c0ce7974be520":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/candidates/the-backyard-safari/page2-1.webp","bytes":75610,"type":"image/webp"},"sha256:534b5ad9449fecf8198ed68a668d4e09df010c081dd8a0b3637ffe7b2b3fef08":{"path":"/story-spark-preview/audio/534b5ad9449f.mp3","bytes":59181